 For a logical pair at physical ray indices i<j and distance d=j-i, move the first label to j-1 by d-1 consecutive full SWAPs, apply the gate on j-1,j with the transported control/target orientation, and reverse those d-1 SWAPs. The whole word is exactly the intended pair gate on its original factors and identity on every intermediate factor. Thus it costs 2d-1 physical gates. The operator proof works on arbitrary dirty, correlated transit factors. A transit site may belong to another leaf set or already contain garbage; every completed route restores it before another logical gate begins. Original D/S factors are never memory-compression transit.
